## 3. Hardware and Software

An embedded system needs both to work.

- **Hardware:** the physical components. For example, the [STM32F411RET6](https://www.st.com/en/microcontrollers-microprocessors/stm32f411re.html) **microcontroller** (an integrated circuit) on the **NUCLEO-F411RE** board, which makes setup and configuration easy.
- **Software (firmware):** the program loaded into the hardware that makes it do its job.

Most devices around you contain an embedded system, which is why these constraints shape so much of modern engineering.

